title: Renew a claim when its holder claims it again
created: 2026-10-24T09:52:25Z
updated: 2026-10-24T09:52:25Z
effort: S
area: cli
handoff:

Ported from a downstream project's vendored copy, where it was found and fixed.

The docs say an agent renews a lease by claiming again, but claim refused
it: a lease's runtime is `-`, which never matches this machine's, so the
agent's own live lease read as unverifiable ("which this machine cannot
check"). A process claiming a ticket it already holds was refused the same
way, as "which is running".

Fix: when the claim is live or unverifiable and its holder is the one
asking, renew it (a fresh expiry for a lease) and print `N renewed by
<who>`. Also work out holder and lease_expiry before taking the lock:
both can die, and a die under the lock left it behind.

Done when claim.sh pins renewal of a lease and of a pid claim, the
refusal of a different holder, and no lock left by a bad PIDLY_LEASE or
PIDLY_PID.
